---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.astro";
import {
  BROWSER_STORAGE,
  DATA_CATEGORIES,
  ESSENTIAL_COOKIES,
  PRIVACY_EFFECTIVE_DATE,
  RETENTION_ROWS,
  THIRD_PARTIES,
} from "../data/privacy";
import { LEGAL_INFRASTRUCTURE, LEGAL_OPERATOR, MOLDOVA_AUTHORITY } from "../data/legal";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy — NovaGuard"
  description="Who operates NovaGuard, what data it processes, why, where it goes, how long it is kept and how to exercise your rights."
>
  <Nav />
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5 py-12 sm:px-6 sm:py-20">
    <p class="text-xs tracking-[0.25em] text-ink-muted uppercase">
      Effective {PRIVACY_EFFECTIVE_DATE}
    </p>
    <h1 class="font-display mt-4 text-3xl sm:text-5xl">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
      This policy covers the hosted NovaGuard Discord bot, dashboard and website. It explains who
      is responsible, what is processed, why it is needed, where it goes and how long it remains.
    </p>

    <aside class="mt-8 rounded-lg border border-line bg-card p-5" aria-label="Controller details">
      <p class="font-display text-lg font-semibold">Operator and privacy contact</p>
      <dl class="mt-4 grid gap-3 text-sm sm:grid-cols-[11rem_1fr]">
        <dt class="text-ink-faint">Operator</dt>
        <dd class="text-ink">{LEGAL_OPERATOR.name}, individual operator</dd>
        <dt class="text-ink-faint">Country</dt>
        <dd class="text-ink">{LEGAL_OPERATOR.country}</dd>
        <dt class="text-ink-faint">Contact address</dt>
        <dd>
          <a
            href={`mailto:${LEGAL_OPERATOR.contactAddress}`}
            class="text-ink underline decoration-line-strong underline-offset-4 hover:text-primary"
          >{LEGAL_OPERATOR.contactAddress}</a>
        </dd>
      </dl>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        {LEGAL_OPERATOR.name} controls NovaGuard's hosting, account access, security, support,
        backups and service-level processing. A Discord server administrator separately chooses
        which optional community features are enabled and how they are used in that server. For a
        community-specific concern, contact the server administrator and NovaGuard where relevant.
      </p>
    </aside>

    <aside class="mt-5 rounded-lg border border-line bg-card p-5" aria-label="Privacy summary">
      <p class="font-display text-lg font-semibold">The short version</p>
      <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        NovaGuard has no advertising, does not sell personal data and uses no third-party
        analytics. Ordinary messages and AI questions are not kept as a NovaGuard history. The
        website uses only storage required for security, sign-in, or a theme you explicitly select.
      </p>
    </aside>

    <section class="mt-14 border-t border-line pt-8">
      <p class="text-xs tracking-[0.2em] text-primary uppercase">01 · Scope and responsibility</p>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-3 text-2xl">How processing decisions are made</h2>
      <div class="mt-4 space-y-4 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        <p>
          NovaGuard processes data needed to operate the service, secure accounts, answer support
          requests and deliver features requested by members or server administrators. Depending
          on the activity, the legal basis is providing a requested service, legitimate interests
          in security and reliable community operation, or a legal obligation. Where consent is
          legally required, it can be withdrawn without affecting earlier lawful processing.
        </p>
        <p>
          Server administrators must enable only features their community needs, give members an
          understandable notice before optional logging, AI or behavioral features are used, and
          identify any additional lawful basis required for their own use. NovaGuard does not use
          Discord data for advertising, cross-community profiling or AI-model training.
        </p>
        <p>
          Data comes from Discord, the person using a command, server administrators, configured
          public GitHub repositories and technical request metadata. Discord identifiers and
          requested command fields are necessary for the corresponding feature. Optional logging,
          levels, economy, voice statistics, GitHub and AI can remain disabled. Refusing essential
          dashboard cookies prevents that sign-in flow, but does not itself remove NovaGuard from
          a Discord server.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-14 border-t border-line pt-8">
      <p class="text-xs tracking-[0.2em] text-primary uppercase">02 · Data inventory</p>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-3 text-2xl">Information NovaGuard processes</h2>
      <div class="mt-6 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-line">
        <table class="w-full min-w-[64rem] border-collapse text-left text-sm">
          <thead class="bg-bg-subtle text-ink">
            <tr>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Category</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">What it includes</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Purpose</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Basis</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-line">
            {
              DATA_CATEGORIES.map((row) => (
                <tr class="align-top">
                  <th class="px-4 py-4 font-medium text-ink">{row.name}</th>
                  <td class="px-4 py-4 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">{row.data}</td>
                  <td class="px-4 py-4 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">{row.use}</td>
                  <td class="px-4 py-4 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">{row.basis}</td>
                </tr>
              ))
            }
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-14 border-t border-line pt-8">
      <p class="text-xs tracking-[0.2em] text-primary uppercase">03 · Cookies</p>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-3 text-2xl">Essential cookies only</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        These first-party cookies are not used for advertising or cross-site tracking. They use{" "}
        <code>HttpOnly</code> and <code>SameSite</code> protections, and production cookies travel
        over HTTPS. Because they are strictly necessary for a flow you request, NovaGuard does not
        show a misleading accept/reject banner. Blocking one prevents that flow from working.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-6 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-line">
        <table class="w-full min-w-[42rem] border-collapse text-left text-sm">
          <thead class="bg-bg-subtle text-ink">
            <tr>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Cookie</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Used for</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Purpose</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Lifetime</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-line">
            {
              ESSENTIAL_COOKIES.map((row) => (
                <tr class="align-top">
                  <th class="px-4 py-4 font-mono font-normal text-ink">{row.name}</th>
                  <td class="px-4 py-4 text-ink-muted">{row.when}</td>
                  <td class="px-4 py-4 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">{row.purpose}</td>
                  <td class="px-4 py-4 text-ink-muted">{row.lifetime}</td>
                </tr>
              ))
            }
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h3 class="font-display mt-9 text-xl">Browser storage</h3>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        Two small first-party preferences remember the theme selected on this device. Neither
        contains a Discord identity, and neither is sent with web requests.
      </p>
      <dl class="mt-5 divide-y divide-line border-y border-line">
        {
          BROWSER_STORAGE.map((row) => (
            <div class="grid gap-2 py-4 sm:grid-cols-[12rem_1fr] sm:gap-6">
              <dt>
                <code class="text-sm text-ink">{row.name}</code>
                <span class="mt-1 block text-xs text-ink-faint">{row.lifetime}</span>
              </dt>
              <dd class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">{row.purpose}</dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-14 border-t border-line pt-8">
      <p class="text-xs tracking-[0.2em] text-primary uppercase">04 · Retention</p>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-3 text-2xl">How long data is kept</h2>
      <dl class="mt-6 divide-y divide-line border-y border-line">
        {
          RETENTION_ROWS.map((row) => (
            <div class="grid gap-1 py-4 sm:grid-cols-[1fr_1.1fr] sm:gap-8">
              <dt class="text-sm font-medium text-ink">{row.data}</dt>
              <dd class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">{row.period}</dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        An erased item can remain inside an encrypted backup until that archive expires. A signed
        pseudonymous deletion ledger prevents restored backups from making erased records live
        again. A limited record may be isolated longer where law, a security investigation or a
        legal claim requires it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-14 border-t border-line pt-8">
      <p class="text-xs tracking-[0.2em] text-primary uppercase">05 · Providers and transfers</p>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-3 text-2xl">Where data is processed</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        Primary NovaGuard runtime data is hosted through {LEGAL_INFRASTRUCTURE.hostingProvider} in
        {` ${LEGAL_INFRASTRUCTURE.hostingRegion}`}. Cloudflare protects and serves the website at
        the network edge. Encrypted recovery archives are uploaded to {LEGAL_INFRASTRUCTURE.backupProvider}.
        They are encrypted and authenticated before upload, and Google does not receive the backup
        key. The configured Google Drive account does not currently pin a disclosed storage
        region, so encrypted files and related service metadata may be processed on Google's
        global infrastructure.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        Discord, Cloudflare, Google, GitHub and Anthropic may also process information outside the
        operator's country. Applicable provider contracts and available legal transfer safeguards
        are used where required. No claim is made that every request, support event or encrypted
        backup remains exclusively in Germany or the European Economic Area.
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-6 divide-y divide-line border-y border-line">
        {
          THIRD_PARTIES.map((provider) => (
            <li class="grid gap-1 py-4 sm:grid-cols-[12rem_1fr] sm:gap-6">
              <a
                href={provider.href}
                target="_blank"
                rel="noreferrer"
                class="font-medium text-ink underline decoration-line-strong underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:text-primary"
              >
                {provider.name}
              </a>
              <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">{provider.detail}</p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="your-choices" class="mt-14 scroll-mt-8 border-t border-line pt-8">
      <p class="text-xs tracking-[0.2em] text-primary uppercase">06 · Your rights</p>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-3 text-2xl">Access, export, correction and erasure</h2>
      <div class="mt-4 space-y-4 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        <p>
          Use <code>/privacy export</code> to privately download records tied to your Discord ID.
          Use <code>/privacy delete</code> to receive a final export and erase or anonymise live
          records. A server administrator can use <code>/privacy server-export</code> and{" "}
          <code>/privacy server-delete</code> for server-scoped data. Logging out revokes the
          active Discord OAuth token and removes the dashboard session.
        </p>
        <p>
          Depending on applicable law, you may request information, access, correction, erasure,
          restriction, portability or objection, and may withdraw consent where processing relied
          on it. Email{" "}
          <a
            href={`mailto:${LEGAL_OPERATOR.privacyEmail}`}
            class="text-ink underline decoration-line-strong underline-offset-4 hover:text-primary"
          >{LEGAL_OPERATOR.privacyEmail}</a>{" "}
          to make a request. Do not send passwords, bot tokens or OAuth tokens. NovaGuard may verify control of the
          relevant Discord account or authority over a server and will respond within the period
          required by applicable law, normally within one month where the new Moldovan law or GDPR
          applies.
        </p>
        <p>
          You may complain to the{" "}
          <a
            href={MOLDOVA_AUTHORITY.href}
            target="_blank"
            rel="noreferrer"
            class="text-ink underline decoration-line-strong underline-offset-4 hover:text-primary"
          >{MOLDOVA_AUTHORITY.name}</a>
          at <a
            href={`mailto:${MOLDOVA_AUTHORITY.email}`}
            class="text-ink underline decoration-line-strong underline-offset-4 hover:text-primary"
          >{MOLDOVA_AUTHORITY.email}</a>, or to another competent authority where applicable. You
          also retain the right to seek a judicial remedy.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-14 border-t border-line pt-8">
      <p class="text-xs tracking-[0.2em] text-primary uppercase">07 · Moderation and AI</p>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-3 text-2xl">Automated processing and human review</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        AutoMod applies rules configured by a server administrator and can remove or flag content;
        it is not used to make legal or similarly significant decisions. Appeals and human review
        belong with that server's moderators. The optional <code>/ask</code> command returns an AI
        answer requested by the member; it does not decide access, moderation or legal rights.
        AI output can be inaccurate and must not replace professional advice or a human decision.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-14 border-t border-line pt-8">
      <p class="text-xs tracking-[0.2em] text-primary uppercase">08 · Age</p>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-3 text-2xl">Children and minimum age</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        NovaGuard is available only through Discord and is not directed to anyone below Discord's
        minimum age or the minimum age required by local law. NovaGuard does not request a date of
        birth. If a parent or guardian believes a child used the service below the permitted age,
        contact the privacy address so relevant NovaGuard records can be investigated and erased.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-14 border-t border-line pt-8">
      <p class="text-xs tracking-[0.2em] text-primary uppercase">09 · Security and changes</p>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-3 text-2xl">Safeguards</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        Dashboard OAuth tokens are encrypted at rest, session identifiers are hashed, production
        traffic uses HTTPS, private backups are authenticated and encrypted before upload, changes
        are access-controlled and audited, and erasures are protected across restores. No method
        is completely secure. Report a suspected incident privately to{" "}
        <a
          href={`mailto:${LEGAL_OPERATOR.privacyEmail}`}
          class="text-ink underline decoration-line-strong underline-offset-4 hover:text-primary"
        >{LEGAL_OPERATOR.privacyEmail}</a>{" "}
        before disclosing it elsewhere.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        This policy was prepared for launch in view of Moldova's{" "}
        <a
          href="https://datepersonale.md/legea-nr-195-2024-privind-protectia-datelor-cu-caracter-personal-principalele-prevederi-si-noutati-legislative/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noreferrer"
          class="text-ink underline decoration-line-strong underline-offset-4 hover:text-primary"
        >Law no. 195/2024</a>, which enters into force on August 23, 2026. This does not replace
        continuing operational or legal review. Material changes to purposes, providers, storage
        or rights will be published here with a new effective date and, where required, an
        additional notice.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
